# CleanPlateVA — cache-control for the public data channel, applied by the
# Workers static-assets layer (design ref docs/architecture-v4.md §9,
# D-TRANSPORT-4, CPH-M3). GENERATED by cannon-food's publisher from the
# committed Lite manifest — do not edit by hand; it is rewritten with every
# Lite publish. These rules reach only responses the assets layer serves:
# /data/* is deliberately NOT in wrangler.jsonc's run_worker_first, so the
# basic map and the shared finder (which the full tier also fetches from here
# first, by content-addressed name, R2 fallback on a miss) cost no Worker
# requests. The manifest is the small mutable pointer (P3: revalidate
# quickly). The finder shards are content-addressed (a name changes iff its
# bytes do), so they are cached forever — and they are listed BY NAME rather
# than as /data/finder/*, because a splat rule also stamps `immutable` on the
# SPA shell the assets layer returns for a name the tree lacks (measured on
# production 2026-08-18), which would let a browser or the edge hold that
# shell for a year; an unlisted name falls back to the assets default,
# `max-age=0, must-revalidate`, and the client treats the shell as a miss.

